This isn't entirely on-topic, as it involves playing Rogue from the
perspective of  a NetHack fanatic.  However, since R.G.R.R is
basically dead, I'm posting here.

After ascending a few times with NetHack, I decided to try my hand at
Rogue (you know, for historical context and all that).  I thought
NetHack was challenging, but this game is HARD.  The concept of "any
character is ascendable" that may or may not be true with NetHack is
definitely false with Rogue.  You can die at any moment, and there's
nothing you can do about it.

I've been trying to ascend for about two months, and I've barely made
it past level 20.  There just always seems to be a level where the RNG
decides I've had enough, regardless of how many escape devices I'm
carrying.

Would anyone like to share Rogue ascension experiences?  Can it REALLY
be done?

